
# Password Strength Analyzer

## Introduction
Password Strength Analyzer is a Python-based application that evaluates password strength using basic security checks.

## Aim
To develop a simple tool that analyzes password characteristics and provides suggestions for improving password security.

## Objectives
- Check password length.
- Detect uppercase and lowercase letters.
- Identify numbers and special characters.
- Detect commonly used passwords.
- Calculate a password score.
- Provide security suggestions.

## Technologies Used
- Python 3
- Visual Studio Code
- Windows 11

## Features
1. Password length checking
2. Character type detection
3. Common password detection
4. Password scoring system
5. Strength classification
6. Security suggestions

## Methodology
1. Accept password input.
2. Calculate password length.
3. Identify character types.
4. Compare against a small common-password list.
5. Calculate the password score.
6. Classify password strength.
7. Display the analysis report.

## Test Cases
| Dummy Password | Expected Strength |
|---|---|
| admin | Very Weak |
| hello | Very Weak |
| hello123 | Moderate |
| Hello@123 | Very Strong |

## Result
The program successfully analyzed all four test cases and generated strength classifications and security suggestions.

## Conclusion
This project demonstrates basic password strength evaluation using Python. It provides an understanding of password characteristics and basic security practices.

## Disclaimer
This is an educational project using a simple custom scoring method. It is not a formal password security standard.
